  "response": "```python\nimport heapq\n\ndef shortest_path(edges, start, end):\n    \"\"\"\n    Find the shortest path between two nodes in a directed weighted graph.\n    \n    Args:\n        edges: List of tuples (from_node, to_node, weight)\n        start: Starting node\n        end: Ending node\n    \n    Returns:\n        Tuple (distance, path) where distance is total weight and \n        path is list of nodes along the shortest route\n    \n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If any edge has a negative weight\n    \n    Examples:\n        >>> shortest_path([(\"A\",\"B\",1), (\"B\",\"C\",2), (\"A\",\"C\",5)], \"A\", \"C\")\n        (3, [\"A\", \"B\", \"C\"])\n    \"\"\"\n    # Handle the case where start and end are the same node\n    if start == end:\n        return (0, [start])\n    \n    # Build adjacency list from edges\n    graph = {node: [] for node in set(edge[0] for edge in edges) | \n                     set(edge[1] for edge in edges)}\n    \n    for from_node, to_node, weight in edges:\n        if from_node not in graph:\n            graph[from_node] = []\n        if to_node not in graph:\n            graph[to_node] = []\n        graph[from_node].append((to_node, weight))\n    \n    # Check for negative weights (raises ValueError if found)\n    for from_node, to_node, weight in edges:\n        if weight < 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"Negative weight edge found\")\n    \n    # If either start or end node is not in the graph at all\n    if start not in graph or end not in graph:\n        return (None, None)\n    \n    # Dijkstra's algorithm\n    distances = {node: float('inf') for node in graph}\n    distances[start] = 0\n    pq = [(0, start)]  # Min-heap with (distance, node)\n    came_from = {}  # To reconstruct path\n    \n    while pq:\n        current_dist, current_node = heapq.heappop(pq)\n        \n        # Skip if we've already found a shorter path to this node\n        if current_dist > distances[current_node]:\n            continue\n        \n        # If we've reached the target node, we can stop early\n        if current_node == end:\n            break\n        \n        # Explore neighbors\n        for neighbor, weight in graph.get(current_node, []):\n            distance = distances[current_node] + weight\n            \n            if distance < distances[neighbor]:\n                distances[neighbor] = distance\n                came_from[neighbor] = current_node\n                heapq.heappush(pq, (distance, neighbor))\n    \n    # Check if end is reachable\n    if distances[end] == float('inf'):\n        return (None, None)\n    \n    # Reconstruct path from end to start\n    path = []\n    current = end\n    while current != start:\n        path.append(current)\n        if current not in came_from:\n            break  # Shouldn't happen if we reached the target\n        current = came_from[current]\n    path.append(start)\n    \n    path.reverse()\n    \n    return (distances[end], path)\n```",
